    "answer": {
      "short": "$k=5$. Correct answer: C.",
      "worked": "A spanning tree of 8 vertices has 7 edges. Choosing the smallest edges first, without creating a cycle: the edges of weight $2$ (bottom right), $3$ (top right), $4$ (top left), $5$ (bottom left) and $5$ (vertical in the left square) give two groups on the right and one on the left. The edge of weight $6$ between the top-left and top-middle vertices joins the left group to the right. The edge $k$ joins the two groups on the right, so the other edge of weight $6$ is not needed.\n$$\\begin{align*}2+3+4+5+5+6+k&=30\\\\25+k&=30\\\\k&=5\\end{align*}$$\nCorrect answer: C.",
